CodeBrix patch 0004 - absent bind group slots in pipeline layouts (wgpu-native/src/conv.rs)

WHAT: map_pipeline_layout_descriptor keeps a NULL bindGroupLayouts entry as None (wgpu-core's
PipelineLayoutDescriptor takes Option<BindGroupLayoutId>) instead of dereferencing every entry
(`expect("invalid bind group layout ...")` - a panic, i.e. a process abort). Everything else about
the descriptor is validated by wgpu-core and reported through handle_error (error scopes /
uncaptured-error callback) as before.
WHY: WebGPU's GPUPipelineLayoutDescriptor.bindGroupLayouts is a sequence<GPUBindGroupLayout?>; a
layout such as [null, group1] is legal and used by real applications.
UPSTREAM: no fix exists in gfx-rs/wgpu-native trunk (589e6caa4e) or open PR #630 (both still
`Some(layout.as_ref().expect(..).id)`). CodeBrix's own change; candidate for upstreaming.

--- a/wgpu-native/src/conv.rs
+++ b/wgpu-native/src/conv.rs
@@ -510,16 +510,12 @@ pub(crate) unsafe fn map_device_descriptor<'a>(
 pub unsafe fn map_pipeline_layout_descriptor<'a>(
     des: &native::WGPUPipelineLayoutDescriptor,
 ) -> wgc::binding_model::PipelineLayoutDescriptor<'a> {
+    // CodeBrix (patches/0004): a NULL entry is an absent bind group slot (WebGPU's entries are
+    // GPUBindGroupLayout?) and stays None for wgpu-core, which validates the layout; it was
+    // dereferenced before (a panic, i.e. a process abort at the C boundary).
     let bind_group_layouts = make_slice(des.bindGroupLayouts, des.bindGroupLayoutCount)
         .iter()
-        .map(|layout| {
-            Some(
-                layout
-                    .as_ref()
-                    .expect("invalid bind group layout for pipeline layout descriptor")
-                    .id,
-            )
-        })
+        .map(|layout| layout.as_ref().map(|layout| layout.id))
         .collect::<Vec<_>>();
 
     let immediate_size = des.immediateSize;
